704. Binary Search

Given an array of integers nums which is sorted in ascending order, and an integer target, write a function to search target in nums. 
If target exists, then return its index. Otherwise, return -1.
You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime comp

Explanation:

keep 2 pointers - left=0 and right=n-1:
if the mid value is equal to target, return the element
if the mid value is greater than the target, shift the right pointer to 1 space before the right ie: mid=right-1;
if mid value is less than the target, shift the left pointer to 1 pointer to left=mid+1;

Code:

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int n=nums.length;
        int left=0;
        int right=n-1;

        while(left<=right){
            int mid=(left+right)/2;
            if(nums[mid]==target){
                return mid;
            }
            else if(nums[mid]<target){
                left=mid+1;
            }
            else if(nums[mid]>target){
                right=mid-1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
